  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Severe thunderstorms capable of damaging winds \nand heavy rainfall remain possible today into this evening.\n\nThe second of two shortwaves embedded in the NW flow of a\ndeepening SE Canada and Ern U.S. trough (will be located across\nthe Upper Glakes at 12Z) and will move quickly SE and bring at \nleast another 1-2 rounds of MDT-HVY SHRA/TSRA across the CWA \ntoday into this evening with localized additional rainfall \namounts of over 2 inches given the rich moisture with PWATS of \n1.5-1.7 inches across all of the CWA. \n\nThe target for the greatest number of SHRA/TSRA is over our SE\nCWA where a FLash Flood Watch was posted and extends through 2\nAM EDT WED. \n\nModels close off the mid and upper low over SE Ont and New York\nState late tonight/Wed. \n\nSome heavy rain potential will linger into Wednesday as the \nslow moving upper low dips over northeast PA/SE NY before\ndrifting East toward southern New England Wed night. 36-48 hour \nstorm total rainfall could exceed 3 inches over some parts of \nthe northeast CWA by Thursday morning.",
